{"dur":90,"ev":[{"t":0.5,"type":"voice","id":"c01"},{"t":8.091,"type":"voice","id":"c02"},{"t":16.418,"type":"voice","id":"c03"},{"t":25.838,"type":"voice","id":"c04"},{"t":31.106,"type":"voice","id":"c05"},{"t":36.346,"type":"voice","id":"c06"},{"t":42.565,"type":"voice","id":"c07"},{"t":50.591,"type":"voice","id":"c08"},{"t":55.941,"type":"voice","id":"c09"},{"t":62.596,"type":"voice","id":"c10"},{"t":67.67,"type":"voice","id":"c11"},{"t":72.896,"type":"voice","id":"c12"},{"t":79.254,"type":"voice","id":"c13"},{"t":82.045,"type":"voice","id":"c14"},{"t":0.5,"type":"sub","d":7.291,"text":"In Ayodhya, King Dasharatha had four sons. The eldest, Rama, was brave, gentle, and true to his word."},{"t":8.091,"type":"sub","d":8.027,"text":"In Mithila, Princess Sita would marry whoever could string the mighty bow of Shiva. Rama lifted it, and it snapped in two."},{"t":16.418,"type":"sub","d":9.12,"text":"But on the eve of his crowning, Queen Kaikeyi claimed two old promises: her son Bharata as king, and Rama exiled for 14 years."},{"t":25.838,"type":"sub","d":4.968,"text":"Rama left without anger. Sita and his brother Lakshmana walked beside him."},{"t":31.106,"type":"sub","d":4.94,"text":"Bharata would not take the throne. He placed Rama's sandals upon it, and waited."},{"t":36.346,"type":"sub","d":5.919,"text":"In the forest, a golden deer appeared. Rama chased it, but it was a demon in disguise."},{"t":42.565,"type":"sub","d":7.726,"text":"Then Ravana, king of Lanka, seized Sita in his flying chariot. The brave vulture Jatayu fought him, and fell."},{"t":50.591,"type":"sub","d":5.05,"text":"Searching for her, Rama found friends: the monkey king Sugriva, and Hanuman."},{"t":55.941,"type":"sub","d":6.355,"text":"Hanuman leapt across the sea, gave Sita Rama's ring, and set Lanka ablaze with his burning tail."},{"t":62.596,"type":"sub","d":4.774,"text":"The army built a bridge of floating stones, each one marked with Rama's name."},{"t":67.67,"type":"sub","d":4.926,"text":"After a long war, Rama's arrow struck Ravana down, and Sita was free."},{"t":72.896,"type":"sub","d":6.058,"text":"They came home to Ayodhya, where every road was lit with lamps, and Rama was crowned at last."},{"t":79.254,"type":"sub","d":2.491,"text":"Every Diwali, those lamps are lit again."},{"t":82.045,"type":"sub","d":2.103,"text":"Rama: the one who kept his word."},{"t":0.7,"type":"pencil","d":0.8},{"t":0.1,"type":"panel","k":0,"d":7.590999999999999},{"t":7.591,"type":"brush","d":0.8,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.9,"pan1":0.9},{"t":8.291,"type":"pencil","d":0.8},{"t":7.691,"type":"panel","k":1,"d":8.327},{"t":15.918,"type":"brush","d":0.8,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.9,"pan1":0.9},{"t":16.618,"type":"pencil","d":0.8},{"t":16.018,"type":"panel","k":2,"d":9.420000000000002},{"t":25.338,"type":"brush","d":0.8,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.9,"pan1":0.9},{"t":26.038,"type":"pencil","d":0.8},{"t":25.438,"type":"panel","k":3,"d":5.268000000000001},{"t":30.606,"type":"brush","d":0.8,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.9,"pan1":0.9},{"t":31.306,"type":"pencil","d":0.8},{"t":30.706,"type":"panel","k":4,"d":5.239999999999995},{"t":35.846,"type":"brush","d":0.8,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.9,"pan1":0.9},{"t":36.546,"type":"pencil","d":0.8},{"t":35.946,"type":"panel","k":5,"d":6.219000000000001},{"t":42.065,"type":"brush","d":0.8,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.9,"pan1":0.9},{"t":42.765,"type":"pencil","d":0.8},{"t":42.165,"type":"panel","k":6,"d":8.026000000000003},{"t":50.091,"type":"brush","d":0.8,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.9,"pan1":0.9},{"t":50.791,"type":"pencil","d":0.8},{"t":50.191,"type":"panel","k":7,"d":5.350000000000001},{"t":55.441,"type":"brush","d":0.8,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.9,"pan1":0.9},{"t":57.641,"type":"pencil","d":0.8},{"t":55.541,"type":"panel","k":8,"d":6.654999999999994},{"t":62.096,"type":"brush","d":0.8,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.9,"pan1":0.9},{"t":62.796,"type":"pencil","d":0.8},{"t":62.196,"type":"panel","k":9,"d":5.074000000000005},{"t":67.17,"type":"brush","d":0.8,"g":0.35,"pan0":-0.9,"pan1":0.9},{"t":67.87,"type":"pencil","d":0.8},{"